  "changes": [
    "PASSIVE tracks each enemy and caster independently: genuine basic/ability HP or shield loss opens a two-second melee opener; the first in-range hit gains one finite bonus, with an eight-second per-target lock. Four seconds without combat are needed to re-engage; ongoing combat cannot renew the opening window.",
    "Q moves one grounded unit, then strikes one forward arc from the actual endpoint. It no longer jumps or pushes targets.",
    "W adds finite armor and magic resistance for three seconds through one stack key. Recasting refreshes rather than stacking; expiry restores ordinary damage.",
    "E is a harmless grounded approach: wall or first enemy body stops it. It does not inherit damage, push or leap from the former charge template.",
    "R has a 0.55-second interruptible windup, then a bounded straight dash. Wall-permitted displacement is swept for the first legal enemy and stops at contact before one damage payload. Ties use entity ID; allies, dead bodies, other zones, behind-wall and behind-direction bodies do not qualify. Existing soft body separation and GGD speed caps remain; authored speed 22 resolves to current runtime cap 16.",
    "EX requires the target to have the caster own two-second recent-hit mark and be within three units. It consumes one mark at acceptance, delivers one extra strike, and refuses out-of-range use without approach, mana, cooldown or mark expenditure.",
    "Generic opt-in fields are allowApproach, dash.stopOnHit/onHit and damageConnected. Deferred contact keeps exact dash identity and cast context; zero-direction reuse, death and replacement cannot inherit a stale contact payload.",
    "Editor preview earns EX eligibility through a real prior Q or R hit. Empty preview and the harmless E step cannot manufacture the mark; the source project remains unchanged."
  ],
